Package: Rfishmorph
Type: Package
Title: The FISHMORPH Reference Database and the Visualisation of Its Functional Space
Version: 0.18.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aurele", "Toussaint", email = "aurele.toussaint@cnrs.fr",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(affiliation = "CNRS")))
Description: Tools dedicated to the FISHMORPH morphological database (Brosse et
    al., 2021, Global Ecology and Biogeography). Rfishmorph reconstructs the 21
    FISHMORPH landmarks, computes the 11 body segments and the 9 dimensionless
    morphological ratios, standardizes landmark geometry and enforces the
    FISHMORPH digitizing conventions, projects specimens into the FISHMORPH
    functional trait space, and provides visualization and quality-control tools
    to compare segment- and landmark-derived measurements. It also offers a
    guided workflow to add new species, using 'rfishbase' to validate and update
    taxonomy and to build a global list of freshwater fishes. It owns the
    visualisation of the FISHMORPH functional space -- static and interactive
    ('plotly') projections, density curves, the ordination engine shared with
    'intraitR' -- and two 'shiny' applications: an explorer of the global
    morphological space of freshwater fishes, and a drainage-basin explorer that
    reads that space through a world map of basins, their species composition
    and their functional-diversity indices. Measuring (the landmark digitizer,
    its journal and its database) belongs to 'intraitR'.
